{:adr-id "2607154312"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-4312 (site preparation) site-preparation-project-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607155000" "ADR-2607150700" "ADR-2607011000" "ADR-2607142800" "ADR-2607152000"]

 :context
 "cloud-itonami-isic-4312 did not exist prior to this ADR (verified via gh api
  repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4312 404 before starting -- no failed prior
  attempt to recover from). ISIC Rev.5 class 4312 is Site preparation (excavation,
  earth-moving, land clearing, test drilling/boring/core sampling) -- confirmed
  against the authoritative kotoba-lang/industry registry (id 4312 = 'Site
  preparation', maturity :spec) before scaffolding, avoiding the code-mislabel
  failure mode earlier ADRs in this batch (e.g. ADR-2607154000, isic-0145) had to
  guard against. A safety-critical domain distinct from sibling 4311 (Demolition):
  the primary risks are excavation collapse and buried-utility strike, not structural
  collapse or hazmat exposure. cloud-itonami-isic-4311 (Demolition) was read in full
  as the primary structural template -- itself a deliberately-narrowed,
  coordination-only sibling of cloud-itonami-isic-4211 (the fleet's robotics-premise
  reference), and its module shape (facts/governor/notify/operation/phase/registry/
  sim/store + advisor) transfers directly to the site-preparation domain. Like 4311,
  this task explicitly required a NARROWER design than 4211: site preparation is
  construction/heavy-equipment-adjacent, so per this workspace's standing rule
  against new Rust/robot-control code, cloud-itonami-isic-4312 was scoped
  coordination-only from the start -- no robotics/simphysics analog, no module
  committing a real-world actuation effect. Every proposal carries :effect :propose
  unconditionally; the governor HARD-holds anything else -- the same permanent
  structural invariant ADR-2607155000 established for 4311. Built by reading
  cloud-itonami-isic-4311 in full, adapting its module shape to the site-preparation
  domain (demolition.* -> site-prep.*, hazmat-survey -> utility-locate,
  demolition-notification -> excavation-notification, :schedule-demolition-operation
  -> :schedule-site-operation), researching REAL regulatory citations for JPN/USA/DEU
  via web search before writing (never fabricated), with clojure -M:test
  independently re-run before and after every push, matching the stricter
  verification protocol of the preceding ISIC-coverage batch."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["excavation/earth-moving-equipment control (dispatching or commanding equipment)
   -- outside this actor's authority entirely; the closed op-allowlist cannot
   express it, and the governor's forbidden-action-class HARD check independently
   rejects any proposal carrying an :equipment-control?/:direct-actuation? marker,
   un-overridable by any human approval"
  "geotechnical/site-readiness sign-off authority -- the licensed engineer / site
   supervisor's exclusively; :schedule-site-operation proposes a phase-window
   schedule, never a sign-off; the same forbidden-action-class check rejects a
   :finalizes-geotechnical-signoff? marker"
  "real-world actuation of any kind -- every committed record carries :effect
   :propose only (effect-not-propose HARD check, defense-in-depth against a
   compromised/malfunctioning advisor)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-4312 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Notify,
  Advisor, Phase, Operation, Sim (structured after cloud-itonami-isic-4311
  module-for-module, narrowed to coordination-only authority):
  - Governor (Site Prep Governor): 8 hard checks (unknown-op, effect-not-propose,
    forbidden-action-class, site-not-verified, legal-basis-missing,
    utility-locate-incomplete, notification-lead-time-insufficient [quantitative
    jurisdictions only], unresolved-safety-concern) + high-stakes escalation
    (:flag-safety-concern and :schedule-site-operation ALWAYS escalate
    unconditionally at every phase; :order-supplies escalates above a $5000 USD cost
    threshold or below the 0.6 confidence floor)
  - Facts: per-jurisdiction (JPN/USA/DEU) utility-locate/excavation-notification
    legal-basis catalog, citing REAL official sources verified via web search before
    writing: Japan's 労働安全衛生規則第355条 (pre-excavation investigation duty) +
    騒音規制法第14条 (7-calendar-day notice for specified construction work incl.
    backhoe/bulldozer), USA's OSHA 29 CFR 1926.651(b) + the national 811 one-call
    system (honestly labeled a widely-adopted state-law convention, >=2 business
    days, NOT a single federal statute -- unlike 4311's federal NESHAP rule),
    EU/Germany's DIN 4124:2012-01 excavation/trench standard + duty-of-care utility
    query (honestly :qualitative, no fabricated numeric lead-time).
    notification-lead-insufficient? is the same three-valued ground-truth recheck
    family construction.facts/weather-threshold-exceeded? and demolition.facts/
    notification-lead-insufficient? established
  - Registry: pure-function site-record-log/schedule-proposal/safety-concern-flag/
    supply-order-proposal drafts (jurisdiction-scoped sequence numbering) +
    render-safety-concern-notice (human-readable document, legal basis inline,
    explicitly disclaims geotechnical/site-readiness sign-off authority)
  - Store: Store protocol, dual MemStore/DatomicStore (langchain.db), contract-tested
    for parity. DatomicStore uses langchain-store.core (ADR-2607141600) for the
    EDN-blob codec/identity-schema/event-log pattern via a data-driven entity
    field-spec instead of hand-rolling enc/dec*. Unlike every sibling actor, no
    history is double-actuation-guarded -- every op may recur any number of times
    per site, since this actor never actually dispatches/authorizes/files/hands over
    anything
  - Notify: mail+phone (Resend+Twilio) Notifier protocol, structurally identical to
    demolition.notify but fires only after human approval of :flag-safety-concern
    (never on an auto-commit path)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + deterministic mock-advisor (default) + llm-advisor
    (real-inference seam), all four ops carry :effect :propose
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate; :log-site-record/:order-supplies are the ONLY ops ever
    in a phase's :auto set (phase 3); :schedule-site-operation/:flag-safety-concern
    permanently absent from every phase's :auto set
  - Operation: langgraph-clj StateGraph actor, real interrupt-before human-in-the-loop
    + checkpoint resume, structurally identical to demolition.operation
  - Sim: demo driver (clojure -M:dev:run), 8 seeded sites, full episode + six distinct
    HARD-hold paths + cross-jurisdiction (USA) + qualitative (DEU/EU) walkthrough
  - Operations: log-site-record (excavation-progress/soil-test/utility-locate data
    logging, auto-eligible), schedule-site-operation (ALWAYS escalates),
    flag-safety-concern (ALWAYS escalates), order-supplies (cost-threshold-gated)
  - Tests: 68 tests / 253 assertions, all green
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop in src), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - README/GOVERNANCE/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY domain-adapted for
    site-preparation coordination"

